NV_PK(22,{"this gate on nanmen road is the way into the temple its plaque reads first academy of taiwan the stone set in the wall beside it is the dismount stele":"","look out through the dacheng gateway across the road stands the stone pangong arch it was once the temple's outer entrance until nanmen road cut it off":"","this is the gate of entering virtue the door to the old school students walked through it to study the name reminds them that learning starts with being good":"","this small gate on the lawn is the gate of rites its twin is called the path of righteousness the wall between them is gone but the names still remind us to be polite and do what is right":"","dacheng gate leads to the main hall instead of painted door gods its doors have rows of golden studs and its columns have no couplets":"","this granite memorial was set up in 1918 bronze plaques on its sides tell how the temple was repaired and how people gave money for new ritual vessels and instruments":"","in 1918 tainan people gave money to make new bells and other instruments so the confucius ceremony could have proper music again this bronze plaque records it":"","which gate did students walk through to go to school":"","which photo shows the 1918 memorial for new ritual instruments":""});